  <title>Display settings</title>
  <p>
    Configure braille wrapping, contraction, and indicator dots.
  </p>
  <p>
    You can toggle contracted braille using a standard keyboard or a braille display. See
    Braille output for how their bindings are configured.
  </p>
  <section id="settings-display-settings">
    <title>Settings</title>
    <p>
      <em style="strong">Preferences location:</em>
      <gui>Braille</gui> category, <gui>Display Settings</gui> group.
    </p>
    <p>
      <em style="strong">Available settings:</em>
    </p>
    <list>
      <item>
        <p>
          <gui>End of line symbol</gui>: Controls whether
          Orca shows the end-of-line indicator at the end of each line of text. Default: on.
        </p>
      </item>
      <item>
        <p>
          <gui>Word wrap</gui>: Controls whether Orca
          adjusts displayed text so only full words are shown. When word wrap is off, Orca uses
          all available cells so more text can be shown at once. Default: off.
        </p>
      </item>
      <item>
        <p>
          <gui>Contracted Braille</gui>: Controls whether
          Orca uses contracted braille through liblouis, a braille translation library. Default:
          off.
        </p>
      </item>
      <item>
        <p>
          <gui>Expand word at cursor</gui>: When contracted
          braille is enabled, controls whether the word at the cursor is shown in uncontracted
          computer braille, which represents characters individually rather than using
          contractions. Default: on.
        </p>
      </item>
      <item>
        <p>
          <gui>Contraction Table:</gui> Selects the liblouis
          translation table Orca uses for braille symbols and contractions. Default: chosen for
          your locale.
        </p>
      </item>
      <item>
        <p>
          <gui>Indicators</gui>: Controls which braille
          dots Orca uses to mark links, selections, and text attributes. These indicators are
          shown like underlining on the braille display.
        </p>
        <list>
          <item>
            <p>
              <gui>Hyperlink:</gui> Selects the dot or
              dots Orca uses to mark text that is part of a link. Choices: None, Dot 7, Dot 8,
              Dots 7 and 8 (default).
            </p>
          </item>
          <item>
            <p>
              <gui>Selection:</gui> Selects the dot or
              dots Orca uses to mark selected text. Choices: None, Dot 7, Dot 8, Dots 7 and 8
              (default).
            </p>
          </item>
          <item>
            <p>
              <gui>Text Attributes:</gui> Selects the dot or
              dots Orca uses to mark text attributes, such as bold. Choices: None (default), Dot
              7, Dot 8, Dots 7 and 8.
            </p>
          </item>
        </list>
      </item>
    </list>
  </section>
